          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: गुटिका",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "गुटिका — guṭikā — \"a pill\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "प्रतिदिनं द्वे गुटिके खादतु। pratidinaṃ dve guṭike khādatu. Take two pills every day."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feminine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "गुटिका (guṭikā) MW's first sense is \"a small globe or ball\" and then \"a pill\"; MW gives no derivation, so its origin is uncertain (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
